      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Cloud Monitoring**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Monitoring as the data provider. The next step is to get the Google Cloud Monitoring client set up within the script. I am currently working on implementing the API calls needed to retrieve the metric data over the specified window, and I am leaning towards using the client library to interact with the API.\n\n\n**Defining the API Interaction**\n\nI'm now fully committed to using Google Cloud Monitoring, specifically the Python client library. My focus is on the `query_metric_window.py` script. The API interaction is the next hurdle. I'm building a function with `project_id`, `metric_type`, `end_time`, and `minutes` as parameters. This function will construct the time series query and fetch the data, hopefully successfully.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861142555,
          "start": 1789861138645
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc0990d5001Ydnfyb0Xn05b5M",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc098be6001XXipU0u8k06bbC",
      "session_id": "ses_f43f674a9ffelmoHoojKz1q4l7",
      "time_created": 1789861138645,
      "time_updated": 1789861142556
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "e5bi6H0DTYY18MgB",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import monitoring_v3\nfrom google.protobuf.timestamp_pb2 import Timestamp\nimport datetime\n\ndef query_metric_window(project_id: str, metric_type: str, end_time: datetime.datetime, minutes: int):\n    \"\"\"Queries recent datapoints for a named metric over a time window.\n\n    Args:\n        project_id: Your Google Cloud project ID.\n        metric_type: The full metric type (e.g., \"compute.googleapis.com/instance/cpu/usage_time\").\n        end_time: The end time for the query window.\n        minutes: The number of minutes to go back from the end_time.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = monitoring_v3.MetricServiceClient()\n    project_name = f\"projects/{project_id}\"\n\n    start_time = end_time - datetime.timedelta(minutes=minutes)\n\n    # Convert datetime objects to Timestamp protobuf objects\n    end_timestamp = Timestamp()\n    end_timestamp.FromDatetime(end_time)\n    start_timestamp = Timestamp()\n    start_timestamp.FromDatetime(start_time)\n\n    interval = monitoring_v3.TimeInterval(\n        end_time=end_timestamp,\n        start_time=start_timestamp\n    )\n\n    query_params = {\n        \"name\": project_name,\n        \"filter\": f'metric.type = \"{metric_type}\"',\n        \"interval\": interval,\n        \"view\": monitoring_v3.ListTimeSeriesRequest.TimeSeriesView.FULL,\n    }\n\n    print(f\"Querying metric '{metric_type}' for project '{project_id}' from {start_time} to {end_time}...\")\n\n    results = client.list_time_series(request=query_params)\n\n    for time_series in results:\n        print(f\"Metric: {time_series.metric.type}\")\n        print(f\"Resource: {time_series.resource.type}\")\n        for point in time_series.points:\n            print(f\"  Value: {point.value.double_value}, Time: {point.interval.end_time.ToDatetime()}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Example Usage: Replace with your project ID and a valid metric type\n    # For example, to get CPU usage time for a GCE instance:\n    # project_id = \"your-gcp-project-id\"\n    # metric_type = \"compute.googleapis.com/instance/cpu/usage_time\"\n    # end_time = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)\n    # query_metric_window(project_id, metric_type, end_time, 60) # Last 60 minutes\n    print(\"To run, please uncomment the example usage in __main__ and replace with your project_id and metric_type.\")\n    print(\"Ensure you have authenticated with Google Cloud, e.g., using `gcloud auth application-default login`.\")\n",
            "filePath": "query_metric_window.py"
          },
